# URL and network security

Linkagram processes untrusted external URLs.

- Never use WebView to resolve a URL.
- Never enable JavaScript for URL processing.
- Keep HTTP redirects disabled in the client; follow them manually.
- Enforce a redirect limit.
- Detect redirect loops.
- Enforce network timeouts.
- Do not weaken TLS checks or disable hostname verification.
- Do not print full user URLs in release logs.
- Do not persist user URL history unless the feature explicitly requires it.
- Treat redirect chains as potentially sensitive data.
- Handle malformed URLs safely; invalid input must not crash the app.
- Prefer mocked HTTP responses in unit tests; do not call real external hosts.
